findings.description:
The CLI and MCP each implement the same steps:
- building `scopeViews` with the `fileSlice` override and choosing check vs checkAll (workflowTools.ts:276-281; check.ts:173-177);
- resolving the invoking checkout for multi-view fix (workflowTools.ts:266-274; check.ts:233-242);
- running `planRoutedFixes` then `applyFixPlan` (workflowTools.ts:290-295; check.ts:247-252, 281).

The two copies must agree on error handling and on when the invoking checkout is resolved. CLAUDE.md prohibits duplicated logic, and the codebase already shares this kind of step through `buildAttributedViews` and `runAttributed` (mergeCheckResults.ts:31, 71).

Fix: move "scope, check, resolve invoking, plan" into one core function. Each consumer keeps its own prompt and error mapping.
